00:21:35.000 --> 00:22:13.000
That instead of criminalizing people for crossing a border, we should instead fear the society in which we deny a desperate person aid, leaving them stranded on the side of a desert road, much like John did with that young man years ago in the Anza Borrego desert. To put it even more simply, John says we should open our borders. Open borders is not no borders. I do think it makes sense to draw some sort of line around a community in which you say that these people are part of this Commonwealth and these people are part of the other. I think that's just, you know, political organizing.
