36
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:51.000
But the presumption would be, in the version of Open Borders I'm talking about, that that line can be crossed and anyone can do it and they don't need a compelling reason to do so. This idea might sound radical now, but it wasn't always that way. Even Ronald Reagan called for what sounds like an open border between the U.S. and Mexico at a Republican presidential primary debate in 1980. Rather than making them or talking about putting up a fence, why don't we work out some recognition of our mutual problems, make it possible for them to come here legally with a
