work permit. And then while they're working and earning here, they pay taxes here. And when they go on to go back, they can go back and they can cross and open the border both ways. Not long after, The Wall Street Journal called for a five word amendment to the Constitution. There shall be open borders. And less than a decade ago, Democrats running in their party's presidential primary were competing over who is more pro-immigrant.
工作许可。然后当他们在这里工作和赚钱时，他们在这里纳税。当他们准备回去时，他们可以回去，并且可以双向跨越和开放边界。不久之后，《华尔街日报》呼吁对宪法进行一项五个字的修正案。那就是：应当开放边界。就在不到十年前，在其党内总统初选中竞选的民主党人还在争论谁对移民更友善。

